+Optimistic concurrency: pass `expected_revision` to guard against lost updates — the call only succeeds if the memory's current `revision` (returned by memory_get) equals the token. If it doesn't match, the call returns `-32000` with `data.code="update_conflict"` and `data.current_revision` so the caller can retry with fresh data. The response always includes the new `revision`; pass it on the next expected_revision to chain updates safely. Conflicts are also raised when the target has been superseded (returns `data.current_id` of the current version in the chain).""",
